{"id": "EUVD-2026-96904", "enisaUuid": "4ff13a59-3cf7-35bb-962f-f5d39d6d4caf", "description": "Traccar 5.7 through 6.16.0 contains a cross-site request forgery vulnerability that allows attackers to log victims into attacker-controlled accounts because the OpenID Connect callback never validates the OAuth state parameter. Attackers can induce a victim's browser to load /api/session/openid/callback with their own authorization code, causing data the victim enters, such as registered devices, to land in the attacker's account.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T12:19:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T11:53:06", "baseScore": 2.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind/traccar-oidc-client-missing-state-login-csrf", "https://github.com/traccar/traccar/blob/cfab560c79ee9c9eaa41c79c6df351e820d6284b/src/main/java/org/traccar/database/OpenIdProvider.java#L110-L198", "https://github.com/traccar/traccar/blob/cfab560c79ee9c9eaa41c79c6df351e820d6284b/src/main/java/org/traccar/api/resource/SessionResource.java#L175-L193", "https://github.com/traccar/traccar", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/traccar-5.7-through-6.16.0-login-csrf-via-openid-connect-callback"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jf89-8gjp-j4c9", "CVE-2026-108738"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.11, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "9919d7ea-fa7f-32e4-acea-ae0906b1bbd7", "product": {"name": "traccar", "vendor": {"name": "traccar"}}, "product_version": "5.7 \u22646.16.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "16ff1d5f-b250-3371-864d-e1ed13d917b2", "vendor": {"name": "traccar"}}], "isExploited": false}